The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
section = bfd_get_section_by_name(abfd, ".text");
if (section)
    dso->text_offset = section->vma - section->filepos;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the calculation of `dso->text_offset` relies on the `filepos` of the `.text` section in the debug file. If the debug file has been stripped of non-debug sections or has a different file alignment, the `filepos` may not be valid, leading to an incorrect or empty `.text` section and thus incorrect symbol resolution.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < symbols_count; ++i) {
    if (!strcmp(bfd_asymbol_name(symbols[i]), "__ImageBase") ||
        !strcmp(bfd_asymbol_name(symbols[i]), "__image_base__"))
        break;
}
if (i < symbols_count) {
    dso->text_offset = section->vma - (u32)section->vma;
    dso->text_offset += (u32)bfd_asymbol_value(symbols[i]);
} else {
    dso->text_offset = section->vma - section->filepos;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check for the `__ImageBase` symbol, which provides the correct base address for the PE file. By using this base address along with the high bits of the `.text` section's virtual memory address (`vma`), the calculation of `dso->text_offset` becomes accurate, even when the debug file has been stripped or has different alignments. This ensures correct symbol resolution.

